NNAAMMEE
     nnoollooggiinn — disallow logins

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Programs such as login(1) disallow logins if the nnoollooggiinn file exists.
     The programs display the contents of nnoollooggiinn to the user if possible and
     interrupt the login sequence.  This makes it simple to temporarily pre‐
     vent incoming logins systemwide.

     To disable logins on a per-account basis, investigate nologin(8).

SSEECCUURRIITTYY
     The nnoollooggiinn file is ignored for user root by default.

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     The nnoollooggiinn feature is implemented through login.conf(5), which allows to
     change the pathname of the file and to extend the list of users exempt
     from temporary login restriction.

     PAM-aware programs can be selectively configured to respect nnoollooggiinn using
     the pam_nologin(8) module via pam.conf(5).

     The nnoollooggiinn file will be removed at system boot if it resides in _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n
     and _c_l_e_a_n_v_a_r___e_n_a_b_l_e is set to “YES” in rc.conf(5), which is default.
     Therefore system reboot can effectively re-enable logins.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/run/nologin  default location of nnoollooggiinn

